{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.77:0.1", "PA_thag_1.77:0.2", "PA_thag_1.77:0.3"], "en": "Theragāthā 1.77 Ekakanipāta Aṭṭhamavagga (The Eighth Chapter)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.77:0.4"], "en": "The Verses of the Elder Hatthārohaputta:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.77:1.1"], "en": "“Formerly this mind wandered on its journey,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.77:1.2"], "en": "wherever it wished, wherever it desired, as it pleased;”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.77:1.3", "PA_thag_1.77:1.4"], "en": "\"Therefore, today I shall restrain it with wise method, just as a goad-holder restrains a rutting elephant. ...", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.77:1.5"], "en": "[Thus spoke] the Elder Hatthārohaputta.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"}
]
